# The hardware paths the host's own adapters sit over the kept originals of, one family per line: a regex that must match a
# whole libultra name, then the reason. Every other function N64Recomp lists (symbol_lists.cpp reimplemented_funcs and
# ignored_funcs) that the decomp names and that a runtime or host source defines a <name>_recomp for goes to the runtime
# (recomp_profile.py derives the list; nothing is kept by name in the profile). A family that matches none stops the build.
osCont\w*	the SI is the host's: the controller hooks wrap osContInit_kept, osContStartQuery_kept, osContStartReadData_kept and osContGetQuery_kept (si_adapter.cpp), so the originals run
osMotor\w*	the pak commands reach the controller pak through the SI path above
osPfs\w*	the pak file system runs over the same kept SI path (osCont*, the pak commands)
(?:__)?osE?Pi\w*	the PI is the host's: pi_adapter.cpp wraps __osPiRawStartDma_kept, so the originals above it run (osPiStartDma, osEPiStartDma, the PI access queue)
osCartRomInit	initialises the PI handle the kept PI path above uses
osCreatePiManager	creates the PI manager thread of the kept PI path above
